# Modelfile.krikri-omega
# Build:  ollama create krikri-omega -f Modelfile.krikri-omega
# Target: Ryzen 7 5700U, ~16 GB RAM, CPU-only (Vega iGPU unused), Ollama 127.0.0.1:11434
# Base:   Llama-Krikri-8B-Instruct (Llama-3.1-8B lineage, 128k native context)
#
# NOTE: Ollama-only. llama-server (:8080) ignores this file, and a request that carries its
# own system message replaces the SYSTEM below. Keep the STACK RULES in the agent prompt layer too.

FROM /home/xnai/models/gguf/Krikri-8b-Instruct-Q5_K_M.gguf

# --- Chat + tool-calling template (Llama 3.1 format) -------------------------------------
# Reconstructed from the Llama 3.1 layout; NOT render-tested. Verify with the tool-call smoke
# test. If `ollama show` on your current tag already lists "tools", delete this block.
TEMPLATE """{{- if or .System .Tools }}<|start_header_id|>system<|end_header_id|>
{{- if .System }}

{{ .System }}
{{- end }}
{{- if .Tools }}

You are a helpful assistant with tool calling capabilities. When you receive a tool call response, use the output to answer the original user question.
{{- end }}<|eot_id|>
{{- end }}
{{- range $i, $_ := .Messages }}
{{- $last := eq (len (slice $.Messages $i)) 1 }}
{{- if eq .Role "user" }}<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
{{- if and $.Tools $last }}

Given the following functions, respond with a JSON for a function call with its proper arguments that best answers the given prompt.

Respond in the format {"name": function name, "parameters": dictionary of argument name and its value}. Do not use variables.

{{ range $.Tools }}
{{- . }}
{{ end }}
{{ .Content }}<|eot_id|>
{{- else }}

{{ .Content }}<|eot_id|>
{{- end }}{{ if $last }}<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>

{{ end }}
{{- else if eq .Role "assistant" }}<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>
{{- if .ToolCalls }}
{{ range .ToolCalls }}
{"name": "{{ .Function.Name }}", "parameters": {{ .Function.Arguments }}}{{ end }}
{{- else }}

{{ .Content }}
{{- end }}{{ if not $last }}<|eot_id|>{{ end }}
{{- else if eq .Role "tool" }}<|start_header_id|>ipython<|end_header_id|>

{{ .Content }}<|eot_id|>{{ if $last }}<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>

{{ end }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}"""

# --- Default system prompt (agents may override per request) -----------------------------
SYSTEM """You are a local coding assistant inside the Omega Stack: sovereign, offline-first, zero telemetry.
You are a model, not an agent persona. Agent identity comes from the agent prompt. Never conflate agents and models.

STACK RULES
- Write Python 3.12-compatible code (containers run 3.12, host runs 3.13+).
- Torch-free: ONNX and GGUF only. Never import torch or transformers.
- No telemetry, cloud SDKs, or outbound network calls.
- Async uses anyio, not raw asyncio. MCP means Model Context Protocol; use FastMCP.
- Read model paths and settings from YAML config (models.yaml). Never hardcode them.
- No bare except. Do not add new stack components unless asked.

OUTPUT RULES
- Zero fluff. Prefer tables, diffs, status reports, and action plans over prose.
- Minimal, idiomatic changes. When fixing code, quote the faulty line, say why, then give the diff.
- For complex refactors, give a 3-5 line plan first. For simple fixes, answer directly.
- Deliver complete code. Never write "omitted for brevity" or leave placeholder bodies.
- Do not invent APIs. If unsure an API exists, write "UNVERIFIED: <name>".
- List every requirement you did not implement under "NOT DONE". Never claim features the code lacks.
- When formatting or restructuring a document, preserve the original wording exactly. Change structure only.
- End multi-step work with: Done / Pending / Files touched / Next."""

# --- Hardware / context ------------------------------------------------------------------
PARAMETER num_gpu 0
PARAMETER num_thread 8
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
PARAMETER num_predict 4096

# --- Sampling (deterministic code; presence_penalty 1.5 removed) -------------------------
PARAMETER temperature 0.1
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 40
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05

# --- Llama 3.1 turn boundaries -----------------------------------------------------------
PARAMETER stop "<|start_header_id|>"
PARAMETER stop "<|end_header_id|>"
PARAMETER stop "<|eot_id|>"

